.7065]]},"source":{"document":"H-1-5219t","date":"2015-07","file":"kodak-vision3-500t-2015.pdf","url":"https://www.kodak.com/content/products-brochures/Film/VISION3-500T-Color-Negative-Film-7219-TECHNICAL-DATA.pdf","sha256":"06eca2287fbaf57a1aeacbb8151bbd48e23aefb30af2114b412e9c1c63f4d1db"},"notes":["CineStill publishes no technical data. CineStill 800T is reported to be Kodak Vision3 500T (5219) with its rem-jet anti-halation backing removed, rated at EI 800 and processed in C-41; this look is the 5219 datasheet curves rated at EI 800 and printed on a colour paper.","The red glow around highlights (halation) is modelled; its radius, threshold and strength are Grainy's choice, not published values.","Read from the July 2015 vector copy (H-1-5219t, kodak-vision3-500t-2015.pdf); the current copy (H-1-5219, revised 3-26, kodak-vision3-500t.pdf) carries the same four plots as raster images, so the vector copy was used for its exact curve paths.","Exposure indexes printed: tungsten (3200 K) 500, daylight 320 with the Wratten 2 / 85 filter; the curves are for 3200 K tungsten, 1/50 s, so balance is tungsten and iso 500.","Characteristic curves: x axis is absolute log exposure in lux-seconds (top axis, -4.0 to 1.0; the bottom axis gives the same range as camera stops, -8 to +8). Densities are from ECN-2 densitometry (the curve plot says Densitometry: ECN-2).","No Log H Ref or grey-card density table is printed, so log_h_ref is null. The sheet says its exposure scale was extended from a 0-4 to a 0-5 log scale (21 steps instead of 20).","Spectral sensitivity: effective exposure 1/25 s, ECN-2, Status M, density 0.2 above D-min; y is log sensitivity (reciprocal exposure in erg/cm2) as printed. The yellow-forming layer (b) is drawn from about 370 to 530 nm, magenta (g) 450 to 600 nm, cyan (r) 500 to 680 nm; the lines stop where Kodak stops them.","Spectral dye density: ECN-2, D-mins subtracted, diffuse density; the cyan, magenta and yellow dye curves are peak-normalised (the c, m and y lines peak at 1.0 as drawn), mid is the Midscale Neutral curve and min the dashed Minimum Density curve. The magenta dye dips slightly below 0 near 450 nm.","Grain: the sheet gives diffuse rms granularity curves only (48 micrometre aperture, ECN-2; Sigma D scale on the right, multiply by 1000), no single printed value, so grain is null. Read by eye from that plot, Sigma D is roughly 0.006 to 0.012 for the green and red records (rms about 6 to 12) and 0.01 to 0.025 for the blue record, depending on density.","Print film: none is named on the sheet; LAD values are said to be specific to each print or duplicating film."],"print":"kodak-endura-premier","derived_from":"kodak-vision3-500t","halation":{"radius":0.004,"threshold":1.0,"strength":[0.35,0.06,0.0]}}